<Defs>
  <!--
  RM_Dustveil: owned RM_ port of the Alpha Animals AngelMoth (sarg.alphaanimals AA_AngelMoth, 1.6/Defs/ThingDefs_Races). Phase 0 step P2 (biome_sprint_kickoff_2026-10-15.md 0.5.3), tool src/RimMandrake/Utils/aa_port.py. Free RM_ tier, home mod TheRot.
  Stats, tools, race fields and pawnkind numbers are the donor's own, as the creature the game shows today
  (our rename/tolerance patches on the donor def are folded in). Departures:
    - wildBiomes dropped (the biome roster casts it); AnimalStatExtension (donor stat defs) dropped.
    - VEF.* comps and VEF_ abilities kept, guarded MayRequire OskarPotocki.VanillaFactionsExpanded.Core (a framework we keep, not the donor).
    - adult art: three owned looks (artpipe angelmoth_option_a/b/c_v1) installed through the art ledger, A at
      RotSpecies/AngelMoth/AngelMoth, B and C as alternateGraphics; larva art from donorart_p2_dustveil_larva_v1.
      No donor picture is reused.
    - dessicated donor art dropped (vanilla fallback).
    - folded 5 op(s) from src/RimMandrake/TheRot/Patches/RotSpecies_NamesAndSizes.xml
    - folded 2 op(s) from src/RimUtinni/UtinniPatches/Patches/AnimalTolerances_Ashkarr.xml
    - folded 3 op(s) from src/RimUtinni/UtinniPatches/Patches/BiomeCastEvictions_WildBiomes.xml
    - leatherDef Leather_Chitin dropped (decoration item; no art owed)
    - customResourceString AA_MothSilkDesc -> 'moth silk' (donor translation key replaced by the words)
    - both eggs draw our Things/Item/RM_AngelMothEggFertilized stack set; the silk draws Things/Item/Resource/RM_MothSilk.
  HAND-OWNED since 2026-10-22 (DUSTVEIL_FLIGHT_BUILD_A_MOTH_THAT_WALKED; owner, by question card, Rot Q5 option 1:
  make the dustveil fly, fungus-grown, no laboratory origin). aa_port.py skips an existing file; never regenerate it.
    - REAL FLIGHT: the MaxFlightTime/FlightCooldown stats plus the race flight fields, in Locust's shape (Odyssey
      Races_Animal_Insect.xml). The flight switch is the stat; VEF Floating stays for water crossing on foot.
    - FLIP-BOOK OWED: the whole-body directional frames (RotSpecies/AngelMoth/Flying/Dustveil_Flying_<N>_<facing>)
      are queued in artpipe and await his look, so flyingAnimationFramePathPrefix is NOT set yet: without it the moth
      flies with no wing-beat (GetBestFlyAnimation returns null); with it and no frames every flight draws pink.
      Set the flyingAnimation* fields on the PawnKindDef when `art install` lands the frames. Never a Spastic
      wing render-tree. One prefix serves all three looks (A, B, C): the frames follow look A.
    - TEXT: every label and description rewritten as a fungus-grown Rot hybrid; the donor's waste-disposal
      origin and the donor art credit (no donor picture ships) are gone. defNames are unchanged (saves).
-->
  <ThingDef ParentName="AnimalThingBase">
    <defName>RM_Dustveil</defName>
    <label>dustveil</label>
    <description>A broad-winged moth of the Rot, grown as much as hatched: its pale wings are a living felt of fungal threads, dusted with spores, and they hang from it like a veil. It flies in short, fluttering hops, over walls and water alike, and drops to the ground to feed. Its grubs are timid things that nibble at sparse growth. The adults are not timid about anything: they eat cloth, wool first and then any natural fibre, worn or stored, and settle for grass only when nothing better is within reach. A tamed one can be shorn of a fine moth-silk, the fungal felt of its wings, provided the silk is kept well away from every other dustveil, which will eat that too.</description>
